# ============================================================================
# CANONICAL fleet / sweep container images — THE SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH.
# ============================================================================
# Every launcher MUST `source` this file and use the variables below. NO script
# may hard-code a `ghcr.io/imazen/...` image literal — scripts/jobsys/check_canonical_images.sh
# FAILS CI if one appears. Variants (cpu / gpu / exec / version) are TAGS on
# these packages, NEVER new package names.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: the worker image was renamed FIVE times in ~8 weeks
#   zen-jobworker -> zen-jobworker-exec -> zenfleet-worker
#     -> zenfleet-worker-exec -> zenfleet-worker-exec-gpu
# and the sweep image FOUR times (zen-metrics-sweep / -salad / -hetzner /
# zenmetrics-sweep). Each rename orphaned the "non-wasteful vastai" capability
# and the next session rebuilt it from scratch. Documentation (the CLAUDE.md
# "ONE ghcr package per artifact" rule) did not stop it because the rename
# happens at `docker build -t`, nowhere near the doc. One file to look at now.
#
# CANONICAL PACKAGES (do NOT invent a 5th — the guard rejects it):
#   zenfleet-worker   job-system worker / executor   (CPU = :latest, GPU = :gpu)
#   zenmetrics-sweep  sweep / score image
#   pycvvdp-scorer    pytorch pycvvdp scorer
#   zen-train         burn trainer
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MIGRATION IN PROGRESS: the working GPU executor still lives under the legacy
# package `zenfleet-worker-exec-gpu`. It must be re-tagged onto
# `zenfleet-worker:gpu` and the legacy package deleted, after which the line
# below changes to that and the guard's MIGRATING exception is removed. Until
# then ZEN_FLEET_IMAGE points at the legacy name so launches keep working.
# 2026-07-02: the plain :exec-gpu tag VANISHED from ghcr (later pushes created only
# variant tags) — 8 fleet boxes sat in "manifest unknown" pull loops. Default now
# points at the newest proven GPU ScoreFile executor tag. When pushing a new GPU
# exec image, ALSO re-tag it :exec-gpu (canonical tags must never be dropped).
# 2026-07-19: rebuilt with current zensim (b79315cfbf4e) + the force-surface
# observability entrypoint; pushed :exec-gpu (canonical) + a pin, and PROVEN on a
# real RTX 3060 (all 6 GPU metrics JIT+ran clean). That pin
# (:exec-gpu-zensim-b79315cfbf4e) is the last GPU-zensim (v1) executor.
# 2026-07-19 (later): GPU zensim kernel DISABLED pending v2 GPU-port validation.
# zensim now extracts on the CPU with the v2 append-only regime (720 = v1-372 ++
# v2-348); the other 5 metrics stay on GPU. Rebuilt zenmetrics @6b3619a621, pushed
# :exec-gpu (canonical) + this v2 pin, PROVEN on a real Titan Xp (5 GPU metrics
# JIT+ran; zensim-gpu returned the CPU value 66.2773, confirming the kernel is
# off). Re-run: `fleet smoke-image <img>`. To revert to v1 GPU zensim, point back
# at :exec-gpu-zensim-b79315cfbf4e (and restore the two zensim fn bodies in code).
# 2026-07-19 (features-only + panic): zensim is now FEATURES ONLY (no score) and
# the GPU zensim kernel is HARD-disabled with an entrypoint panic. Rebuilt
# zenmetrics @0953c94671, pushed :exec-gpu (canonical) + this pin, PROVEN on a real
# RTX 3060 (5 GPU metrics JIT+ran; zensim-gpu is excluded from the smoke because
# `score --metric zensim-gpu` panics by design). Pre-panic image (v2 + score):
# :exec-gpu-zensimv2-6b3619a621.
# 2026-08-24 (CPU only, ZEN_FLEET_IMAGE_CPU): rebuilt with the Nomad-migration P0 fixes
# (JobId #38 + metric routing 1b2a1452, VRAM admission 58c5db95, SIGTERM chunk-claim
# release 0de119d6/45c57bd3, ZEN_MAX_MIN + ZEN_LONG_LIVED 45c57bd3, native claim CAS
# a916d24d). **DISCOVERED + FIXED a real build-pipeline gap while doing this rebuild:**
# `build_executor_image.sh`'s own `cargo build --release -p zenmetrics-cli ...` (dynamic
# glibc) produces a binary requiring whatever glibc the BUILD box happens to run — this
# box had drifted to Ubuntu 26.04 / glibc 2.43, while the base image (`:latest`) is
# Debian bookworm / glibc 2.36, so the resulting binary would refuse to even start
# (`GLIBC_2.43' not found`) despite building and "smoke-testing" fine on the build box
# itself. **Fix: build BOTH `zenmetrics` and `zenfleet-worker` with
# `--target x86_64-unknown-linux-musl` instead** (`rustup target add
# x86_64-unknown-linux-musl` + the `musl-tools` apt package for `musl-gcc`) — fully
# static binaries (`ldd` reports "statically linked"), immune to the base image's libc
# version entirely. **Use the musl target for every future executor rebuild** —
# regardless of what glibc the build box happens to be on that day. Pushed
# :exec-nomad-pilot-2026-08-24 (dated pin) + this canonical :exec pointer, built +
# pushed from r7900x (has docker; this WSL session's own execution environment does not
# have a `docker` binary — see the commit for detail). Smoke-tested: `jobexec --help`,
# `zenfleet-worker --help`, and all 5 baked tools (aws/s5cmd/zenfleet-worker/gunzip/
# timeout) present and runnable inside the image.
# 2026-08-24 (later same day): rebuilt again with diagnostic instrumentation for the
# reopened SIGTERM chunk-claim-release bug (0e998ff3 — see CLAUDE.md Known Bugs /
# benchmarks/fleetbench_2026-08-24.md). zenmetrics binary UNCHANGED (reused the musl
# build from the rebuild above); only zenfleet-worker + fleet-entrypoint.sh rebuilt
# (musl target again) and overlaid. `sudo docker push` failed with "unauthenticated"
# — ghcr credentials live under ~lilith/.docker/config.json, not /root/.docker/, so
# BUILD can use sudo (needed for docker daemon access) but PUSH must run as the plain
# `lilith` user (in the `docker` group, uses its own creds). Pushed
# :exec-gp2-debug-1787549532 (dated pin) + this canonical :exec pointer, smoke-tested
# (jobexec --help, both binaries statically linked).
# 2026-08-27: GPU rebuilt at 399abe82 (all 8 anti-wedge invariants + hdr-gainmap +
# the `capabilities` self-report the claim-time gate probes). GPU zenmetrics built in a
# rust:1-bookworm container (glibc 2.36 <= the v29 base 2.39 — the musl rule's GPU
# counterpart; a host build on Ubuntu 26.04/glibc 2.43 would not start in the image).
# 2026-08-27 (later): :exec-gpu-6d4f9963 is a BLACKWELL TRAP -- it ships ONLY CUDA
# 12.6 (never migrated to the dual-CUDA `docker/base` — see CLAUDE.md "CUDA 12 vs 13
# — selected at RUNTIME, never baked"), and NVRTC 12.6 cannot target sm_120
# (Blackwell, e.g. the wsl RTX 5070): "nvrtc: error: invalid value for
# --gpu-architecture (-arch)", reproduced verbatim. NOT a WSL2 issue — the driver
# advertised CUDA 13.2 fine; only the baked toolkit was too old. Fix:
# :exec-gpu-cuda13-6d4f9963 (zenmetrics 515c21fc) overlays the cuda-13.0 runtime +
# cuda-select.sh (fleet-entrypoint.sh already sources it); Pascal/Turing/Ampere
# boxes keep CUDA 12 automatically via the sm_75-floor rule, so this is a strict
# superset, not a Blackwell-only variant. Smoke-tested live on the wsl RTX 5070
# per the "prove GPU image before repoint" rule (memory: prove-gpu-image-before-
# repoint.md) — real operational CUDA probe passed, real hdrgrid cells scoring.
# Repointed the canonical tag to this overlay so future launches don't hit the
# same trap on any Blackwell card that joins the fleet.
ZEN_FLEET_IMAGE="${ZEN_FLEET_IMAGE:-ghcr.io/imazen/zenfleet-worker:exec-gpu-cuda13-6d4f9963}"
# 2026-08-27: rebuilt at master 399abe82 (anti-wedge invariants 1-7+9: progress-
# conditioned lease renewal, cell deadlines, strict snapshot gate, failure-carrying
# views + sidecar fold, claim-time capability gating incl. `zenmetrics capabilities`,
# cgroup budgets, tolerant readers, store write probe) + hdr-gainmap decode. Built +
# pushed FROM THIS WSL BOX — the 08-24 "this session has no docker binary" note is
# STALE: /usr/bin/docker + daemon (sudo) + user ghcr creds all work here now (push
# via `sudo docker --config ~lilith/.docker push`).
# 2026-08-30: rebuilt at master b5b4b27f-parent (03bdf64b) — adds the ALL-944-LIVE
# feature metric `zensim-foldapp2pools` (regime `folded720append2pools`,
# V1PoolsMode::Full: f156..371 all 216 pool slots live) alongside the existing
# `zensim-foldapp2` / `-foldapp2carriers`. Strict superset of
# exec-zensim944hdr-c0cdf095: same cargo features (sweep,png,jpeg,webp,avif,jxl,
# cpu-metrics,hdr-gainmap), same musl static build, one more metric string.
# VERIFIED on the baked binary, not just at build time: a live 1-cell jobexec run
# inside the image emitted regime=folded720append2pools with 944 features that are
# BIT-IDENTICAL to the same cell scored by the local binary.
# digest sha256:6224582c1bebd7dd4b803d85343d91837019977fc49ca852a71eac663e648d96
# 2026-08-30 (aom lane, NEW TAGS — pins deliberately NOT moved): two images carrying the
# claim-gate + fleet-uniform-chunking fixes were built and pushed. They are RECORDED here
# because this file is the pin ledger, but the pins above are left alone: -03bdf64b is another
# lane's live pin and repointing it mid-run buys this lane nothing (the claim-time capability
# gate now protects every lane regardless of which image is pinned — a wrong-featured executor
# self-excludes LOUDLY instead of claiming and burning the work).
#   :exec-zensim944hdr-d7982e9b   CPU, digest sha256:903eb8d9… (7e4695b3) then rebuilt at
#     d7982e9b. Strict superset of -03bdf64b: same musl static build, PLUS the `avif-svt` +
#     `avif-aom` cargo features (so `zenmetrics capabilities` advertises them and aom-rs/svt-rs
#     encode cells are claimable at all), zenav1-aom cb76cda9f9fe3df6b551fedc86bff568b89b649d
#     (KB-41 roots #22-#23 + KB-42 A-C, tree CLEAN before and after the build), fleet-uniform
#     chunk boundaries, `already_poison=N` on the worker summary, and the `skipped>0 != idle`
#     drain rule. This is the image the aom encode lane now uses.
#   :exec-gpu-cuda13-d7982e9b     GPU, digest sha256:9e7428e6…. A 2-file OVERLAY on
#     :exec-gpu-cuda13-6d4f9963 — the musl `zenfleet-worker` binary + `fleet-entrypoint.sh`
#     only; zenmetrics and the CUDA stack are byte-identical to the base. Built because the
#     base entrypoint counts a `skipped>0` pass as idle: relaunched over 23 cells whose claims
#     were still held by a killed worker's 10-min lease, it ran EIGHT passes in ONE SECOND and
#     exited, twice. With the overlay the same run completed 69/69.
# 2026-08-30 (aom lane, round 3 — pin again deliberately NOT moved): built + pushed
#   :exec-zensim944hdr-8662064f  CPU, digest sha256:72a0b143539b87c80dc106103edf4d42de1327edb6443f359c43cbcd412b9bfa
#     Same shape as -d7982e9b (musl static, avif-svt + avif-aom, fleet-uniform chunking,
#     already_poison=N, skipped>0 != idle) but on zenav1-aom 58204b295dd0 — KB-41 roots
#     #24-#26 — with the sibling tree verified CLEAN both before and after the build.
#     Used for the round-3 requeue of avifaom-enc-20260830: 59 pardoned -> 32 done in one
#     pass per box, 125,941 -> 125,973 distinct done, 27 still failing (14 tiny C3 +
#     13 KB-41 root #27). Record: benchmarks/avifaom_poison_planes_2026-08-30.pointer.md.
#     The pins below stay where they are for the same reason as the 2026-08-30 note above:
#     the claim-time capability gate protects every lane regardless of which image is pinned.
ZEN_FLEET_IMAGE_CPU="${ZEN_FLEET_IMAGE_CPU:-ghcr.io/imazen/zenfleet-worker:exec-zensim944hdr-03bdf64b}"
ZEN_SWEEP_IMAGE="${ZEN_SWEEP_IMAGE:-ghcr.io/imazen/zenmetrics-sweep:latest}"
ZEN_PYCVVDP_IMAGE="${ZEN_PYCVVDP_IMAGE:-ghcr.io/imazen/pycvvdp-scorer:0.5.4}"
